# Each app reads its own file. Copy the block for an app into that app's folder; never commit the copy.
#   apps/mobile/.env   the block below (Expo loads it on `expo start` and `expo export`)
#   apps/web/.env      see apps/web/.env.example (the web pack's own list)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the app bundle: anyone with the app can read them.
# They are never secrets. For EAS builds, set them per environment: `eas env:create`.
# Leave both empty and the app still runs: sign-in is off and no API call leaves the phone.

# Web app origin the mobile app calls for /api/v1 (http://<your-computer's-LAN-IP>:3000 in dev) · get it: the web app's test or production URL · scope: local,test,production · secret: no
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
# Clerk publishable key (the same Clerk application as the web app) · get it: https://dashboard.clerk.com → API keys · scope: local,test,production · secret: no
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
